.TH LEOCAD 1 "October 30, 2026"
.\" NAME should be all caps, SECTION should be 1-8, maybe w/ subsection
.\" other params are allowed: see man(7), man(1)
.SH NAME
LeoCAD \- CAD program for LEGO models.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIleocad \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIINFILE\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fILeoCAD \fR is a CAD program for creating virtual LEGO models. It
has an easy to use interface and includes thousands of different
parts in its library.

.SH OPTIONS
Below is a summary of all of the options that \fILeoCAD\fR
accepts. Many options have two equivalent names, one of
which is a single letter preceded by -, and the other of
which is a long name preceded by --. Brackets ([ and ])
indicate that an option takes an optional parameter.

Colors use RRGGBB or RRGGBBAA hexadecimal notation, with alpha last
and defaulting to FF (opaque). An optional # prefix and the keyword
transparent are also accepted. For example, --background FF000080 selects
half-transparent red. Quote colors with a # prefix in shell commands.

.TP
.B infile
Loads the project file \fIinfile\fR

.TP
\fB\-l \fIpath\fR, \fB\-\-libpath \fIpath
.br
Set the parts library location.

.TP
\fB\-i \fR[\fIoutfile.ext\fR], \fB\-\-image \fR[\fIoutfile.ext\fR]
.br
Save a picture and exit. The format is selected by the output filename
extension and must be supported by the installed image codecs. An explicit
filename without an extension is written as PNG. If the filename is omitted,
use the input name and the saved image extension. Place the input filename
before options with omitted output filenames.

.TP
.BI "\-\-background " color
Set the image background to a color or transparent. Requires --image.
The default is transparent for formats preserving alpha, otherwise white.

.TP
.BI "\-\-background-gradient " "top bottom"
Set a vertical image background gradient using two colors. Requires --image.
Background options cannot be repeated or combined. Formats that do not
preserve alpha require opaque colors.

.TP
\fB\-w \fIwidth\fR, \fB\-\-width \fIwidth
.br
Sets the width of the picture to \fIwidth\fR (1 to 32768).

.TP
\fB\-h \fIheight\fR, \fB\-\-height \fIheight
.br
Sets the height of the picture to \fIheight\fR (1 to 32768).

.TP
\fB\-f \fItime\fR, \fB\-\-from \fItime
.br
Start saving pictures at the step \fItime\fR. Steps start at 1.

.TP
\fB\-t \fItime\fR, \fB\-\-to \fItime
.br
Save pictures until the step \fItime\fR.

.TP
\fB\-s \fIsubmodel\fR, \fB\-\-submodel \fIsubmodel
.br
Sets the active submodel to \fIsubmodel\fR.

.TP
\fB\-c \fIcamera\fR, \fB\-\-camera \fIcamera
.br
Sets the active camera to \fIcamera\fR.

.TP
\fB\-ss \fIid\fR,\ \fB\-\-stud\-style\ \fIid
.br
Set the stud style. Valid values 0=Plain, 1=Thin Lines Logo, 2=Outline Logo,
3=Sharp Top Logo, 4=Rounded Top Logo, 5=Flattened Logo, 6=High Contrast,
7=High Contrast with Logo.

.TP
\fB\-\-viewpoint \fRfront\ |\ back\ |\ left\ |\ right\ |\ top\ |\ bottom\ |\ home
.br
Sets the viewpoint to one of the predefined view angles.

.TP
.BI "\-\-camera\-angles " latitude " " longitude
Set the camera angles in degrees around the model (-360 to 360).

.TP
.BI "\-\-camera\-position " x " " y " " z "  " tx " " ty " " tz "  " ux " " uy " " uz
Set the camera position, target and up vector using the \fILeoCAD\fR
coordinate system.

.TP
.BI "\-\-camera\-position-ldraw " x " " y " " z "  " tx " " ty " " tz "  " ux " " uy " " uz
Set the camera position, target and up vector using the \fILDraw\fR coordinate
system.

.TP
.B \-\-orthographic
Use an orthographic projection.

.TP
.BI "\-\-fov " degrees
Set the vertical field of view used to render images (1 to 180 degrees,
inclusive).

.TP
.BI "\-\-zplanes " near " " far
Set the near and far clipping planes used to render images (1 <= \fInear\fR <
\fIfar\fR).

.PP
Named cameras take precedence over the other camera controls. Otherwise,
viewpoint takes precedence over angles, which take precedence over an explicit
position.

.TP
.B \-\-fade\-steps
Render parts from prior steps faded.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-fade\-steps
Do not render parts from prior steps faded.

.TP
.BI "\-\-fade\-steps\-color " color
Color to use for rendering faded parts. Specifying a color enables fading.

.TP
.B \-\-highlight
Highlight parts in the steps they appear.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-highlight
Do not highlight parts in the steps they appear.

.TP
.BI "\-\-highlight\-color " color
Color to use to highlight parts. Specifying a color enables highlighting.

.TP
\fB\-\-shading \fRwireframe\ |\ flat\ |\ default\ |\ full
.br
Select shading mode for rendering.

.TP
.BI "\-\-line-width " width
Set the width of the edge lines (0 to 10).

.TP
.BI "\-\-aa\-samples " count
Anti-aliasing sample size (1, 2, 4, or 8).

.TP
\fB\-scc \fIRRGGBB|RRGGBBAA|transparent\fR,\ \fB\-\-stud\-cylinder\-color\ \fIRRGGBB|RRGGBBAA|transparent
.br
High contrast stud cylinder color.

.TP
\fB\-ec \fIRRGGBB|RRGGBBAA|transparent\fR,\ \fB\-\-edge\-color\ \fIRRGGBB|RRGGBBAA|transparent
.br
High contrast edge color.

.TP
\fB\-bec \fIRRGGBB|RRGGBBAA|transparent\fR,\ \fB\-\-black\-edge\-color\ \fIRRGGBB|RRGGBBAA|transparent
.br
High contrast edge color for black parts.

.TP
\fB\-dec \fIRRGGBB|RRGGBBAA|transparent\fR,\ \fB\-\-dark\-edge\-color\ \fIRRGGBB|RRGGBBAA|transparent
.br
High contrast edge color for dark color parts.

.TP
\fB\-nscc\fR, \fB\-\-disable\-stud\-cylinder\-color
.br
Disable high contrast stud cylinder color.

.TP
\fB\-nec\fR, \fB\-\-disable\-edge\-color
.br
Disable high contrast edge color.

.TP
\fB\-nbec\fR, \fB\-\-disable\-black\-edge\-color
.br
Disable high contrast edge color for black parts.

.TP
\fB\-ndec\fR, \fB\-\-disable\-dark\-edge\-color
.br
Disable high contrast edge color for dark color parts.

.TP
\fB\-aec,\ \fB\-\-automate\-edge\-color
.br
Enable automatically adjusted edge colors. This overrides manual edge colors;
high contrast stud-cylinder settings still apply.

.TP
\fB\-cc \fIfloat\fR,\ \fB\-\-color\-contrast\ \fIfloat
.br
Set color contrast between 0.0 and 1.0. Requires automatic edge colors.

.TP
\fB\-ldv \fIfloat\fR,\ \fB\-\-light\-dark\-value\ \fIfloat
.br
Set the Light/Dark value between 0.0 and 1.0. Used by automatic edge colors
or as the dark-color threshold for high contrast stud styles.

.PP
Stud-cylinder and manual edge color options require a high contrast stud style
(6 or 7).

.TP
\fB\-obj \fR[\fIoutfile.obj\fR], \fB\-\-export\-wavefront \fR[\fIoutfile.obj\fR]
.br
Exports the model to wavefront format.

.TP
\fB\-3ds \fR[\fIoutfile.3ds\fR], \fB\-\-export\-3ds \fR[\fIoutfile.3ds\fR]
.br
Exports the model to 3DS format.

.TP
\fB\-dae \fR[\fIoutfile.dae\fR], \fB\-\-export\-collada \fR[\fIoutfile.dae\fR]
.br
Exports the model to COLLADA DAE format.

.TP
\fB\-csv \fR[\fIoutfile.csv\fR], \fB\-\-export\-csv \fR[\fIoutfile.csv\fR]
.br
Export the list of parts used in CSV format.

.TP
\fB\-html \fR[\fIpath\fR], \fB\-\-export\-html \fR[\fIpath\fR]
.br
Creates an HTML page for the model.

.TP
.BR \-v ",\ " \-\-version
Output version information and exit.

.TP
.BR \-? ",\ " \-\-help
Display a brief usage synopsis and exit.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
``LEOCAD_LIB'' may be set to the path of the parts library.

.SH EXAMPLES
 $ leocad car.lcd \-i car.png \-w 640 \-h 480
.PP
This will start LeoCAD, load the file "car.lcd," create a png called
"car.png" with a resolution of 640x480 and exit when done.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/LeoCAD Software/LeoCAD.conf
User preferences file

